Here is a step-by-step guide on how to configure Google Tag Manager (GTM) to catch the form submissions from your website and send them to Google Ads as a Conversion.

This is the most accurate and recommended method for tracking Google Ads performance.

Step 1: Get your Conversion Details from Google Ads
First, we need to tell Google Ads to expect a conversion.

Log into your Google Ads account.
Go to Goals > Conversions > Summary.
Click + New conversion action and select Website.
Enter your website domain and scan it. Scroll down and click Add a conversion action manually.
Set the Goal and action optimization to Submit lead form. Name the conversion (e.g., "Landing Page Lead").
Set the value and count (usually "One" for leads) and click Done, then Save and continue.
Under the setup options, select Use Google Tag Manager.
You will see a Conversion ID and a Conversion Label. Keep this page open; you will need these numbers in Step 3.
Step 2: Create a Trigger in Google Tag Manager
Now we tell GTM to "listen" for the specific event our website's code is firing.

Log into Google Tag Manager and select your container (GTM-W5ZSSS8W).
On the left menu, click Triggers, then click New (top right).
Click the Trigger Configuration box and select Custom Event.
Under "Event name", paste exactly this: form_submission_success (This is the exact code we added to the Lead Form).
Name the trigger at the top left (e.g., "Trigger - Lead Form Success") and click Save.
Step 3: Create the Google Ads Tag in GTM
Finally, we connect the Trigger (Step 2) to Google Ads (Step 1).

In GTM, click Tags on the left menu, then click New.
Click the Tag Configuration box and select Google Ads Conversion Tracking.
(Note: If you see a warning that says "Conversion Linker tag missing in container", click the "Create" button it provides to quickly add one. It just takes 2 seconds and is required by Google).
Paste the Conversion ID and Conversion Label you got from Google Ads in Step 1.
Scroll down to the Triggering box at the bottom and click it.
Select the "Trigger - Lead Form Success" trigger you created in Step 2.
Name your tag at the top left (e.g., "Google Ads - Lead Form Conversion") and click Save.
Step 4: Publish
You're done! Click the blue Submit button at the top right of GTM, give your version a name (like "Added Google Ads Tracking"), and click Publish.

Whenever someone successfully submits the form, our code pushes form_submission_success, GTM catches it, and immediately fires a signal back to Google Ads telling it that the ad worked!
